---
import { viewPages } from '../data/views';
import TopNav from '../components/TopNav.astro';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#081b2d" />
    <meta name="description" content="H5Jive is a native scientific data explorer for HDF5 and NetCDF." />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="./h5jive-icon.png" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="./site.css" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="./layout.css" />
    <script src="./carousel.js" defer></script>
    <script src="./releases.js" defer></script>
    <script data-goatcounter="https://h5jive.goatcounter.com/count" async src="//gc.zgo.at/count.js"></script>
    <title>H5Jive — Dig into your data</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <header class="topbar wrap">
      <a class="brand" href="#top" aria-label="H5Jive home"><img class="brand-icon" src="./h5jive.png" width="42" height="42" alt="" /> H5Jive</a>
      <TopNav root="./" home />
    </header>

    <main id="top">
      <section class="hero wrap">
        <div class="hero-top">
          <div class="hero-copy">
            <p class="eyebrow"><span class="pulse"></span> A scientific data explorer</p>
            <h1>Dig into your data.<br /><em>See the whole dataset.</em></h1>
          </div>
          <div class="hero-aside">
            <p class="lede">H5Jive turns HDF5 and NetCDF files into something you can explore: their structure, values, dimensions, and place in the world.</p>
            <div class="hero-actions">
              <a class="button primary" href="#download">Install H5Jive <span>↓</span></a>
              <a class="text-link" href="./browser/">Dataset Browser <span>→</span></a>
              <a class="text-link" href="./features/">Explore features <span>→</span></a>
            </div>
            <div class="hero-meta"><span>BUILT WITH RUST</span><i></i><span>HDF5 · NETCDF</span><i></i><span>NATIVE DESKTOP</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="carousel" role="region" aria-label="H5Jive views" aria-roledescription="carousel">
          <div class="preview carousel-track" id="view-carousel">
            {viewPages.map((shot, i) => <figure class="carousel-slide" aria-label={`${i + 1} of ${viewPages.length}: ${shot.title}`}>
              <div class="map-art"><img src={`./${shot.image}`} width={shot.imageWidth} height={shot.imageHeight} alt={shot.alt} loading={i === 0 ? 'eager' : 'lazy'} fetchpriority={i === 0 ? 'high' : undefined} decoding="async" /></div>
              <figcaption><span><b class="dot"></b> H5JIVE <span class="caption-divider">/</span> {shot.title.toUpperCase()}</span><a href={`./views/#${shot.slug}`}>Explore this view <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></figcaption>
            </figure>)}
          </div>
          <div class="carousel-controls">
            <button class="carousel-arrow" type="button" data-carousel-prev aria-label="Previous view">←</button>
            <div class="carousel-dots" aria-label="Choose a view">
              {viewPages.map((shot, i) => <button class="carousel-dot" type="button" data-carousel-index={i} aria-label={`Show ${shot.title.toLowerCase()} view`} aria-current={i === 0 ? 'true' : undefined}><span></span></button>)}
            </div>
            <button class="carousel-arrow" type="button" data-carousel-next aria-label="Next view">→</button>
          </div>
          <p class="sample-credit">Screenshots show a Band 3 excerpt. Contains modified EUMETSAT Metop-B GOME-2 Level 1B data (2013). © EUMETSAT 2013. <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">CC BY 4.0</a>. Map background: <a href="https://www.naturalearthdata.com/about/terms-of-use/">Natural Earth</a>.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="ticker" aria-label="Supported formats and views"><div class="ticker-inner">HDF5 <b>✳</b> NETCDF <b>✳</b> MULTIDIMENSIONAL ARRAYS <b>✳</b> SCAN PIXEL FOOTPRINTS <b>✳</b> HDF5 <b>✳</b> NETCDF <b>✳</b> MULTIDIMENSIONAL ARRAYS <b>✳</b> SCAN PIXEL FOOTPRINTS</div></section>

      <section id="download" class="downloads wrap">
        <div class="download-heading">
          <div><p class="eyebrow">READY TO RUN</p><h2>Install H5Jive for your account.</h2></div>
          <p>The install scripts fetch a precompiled build, verify its checksum, and keep settings across upgrades. No administrator rights or Rust toolchain needed. <a data-release-page href="https://github.com/vrtulka23/h5jive/releases/latest">See release notes <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></p>
        </div>
        <p class="download-version">Installs the latest published release <span data-release-version></span></p>
        <div class="install-grid">
          <article class="install-card">
            <span>MACOS / LINUX</span>
            <h3>Install from a terminal</h3>
            <pre><code>curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/vrtulka23/h5jive/main/install.sh | sh</code></pre>
            <p>Requires <code>curl</code> and <code>tar</code>. Installs under your home directory and adds a launcher at <code>~/.local/bin/h5jive</code>. The same Linux archive is intended for Ubuntu and openSUSE; it needs a usable Vulkan or OpenGL driver. See the <a href="./guide/getting-started.html#linux-graphics-on-suse">Linux graphics guide</a> if startup reports <code>AdapterUnavailable</code>.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="install-card">
            <span>WINDOWS / POWERSHELL</span>
            <h3>Install for your user</h3>
            <pre><code>curl.exe -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/vrtulka23/h5jive/main/install.ps1 -o "$env:TEMP\h5jive-install.ps1"
powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File "$env:TEMP\h5jive-install.ps1"</code></pre>
            <p>Installs in your user directory and adds H5Jive to your user PATH. Open a new terminal after installing.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
        <p class="download-note"><strong>Signing status:</strong> The Windows installer and executable and Linux AppImage are currently unsigned. The macOS app is ad hoc signed but not Developer ID signed or notarized. Windows may show SmartScreen or “Unknown publisher”; macOS may require additional confirmation on first launch. Linux may require executable permission. Download only from the <a href="https://github.com/vrtulka23/h5jive/releases/latest">official release</a> and check the published SHA-256 checksum.</p>
        <p class="download-note">If macOS blocks H5Jive, try to open it once, then choose <strong>System Settings → Privacy &amp; Security → Open Anyway</strong>. See <a href="https://support.apple.com/en-us/102445">Apple’s instructions</a>.</p>
        <div class="manual-download-heading">
          <h3>Manual downloads</h3>
          <p>Prefer a DMG, AppImage, setup executable, or portable archive? Choose a package below.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="download-grid">
          <article class="download-card">
            <span>WINDOWS / X86_64</span><h3>Windows</h3>
            <p>The setup installer installs for your user account without administrator rights. The ZIP runs from an extracted folder.</p>
            <div class="download-links">
              <a class="download-installer" data-release-asset="h5jive-windows-x86_64-setup.exe" href="https://github.com/vrtulka23/h5jive/releases/latest/download/h5jive-windows-x86_64-setup.exe">Install for this user · .exe ↗</a>
              <a data-release-asset="h5jive-windows-x86_64.zip" href="https://github.com/vrtulka23/h5jive/releases/latest/download/h5jive-windows-x86_64.zip">Download portable ZIP ↗</a>
            </div>
          </article>
          <article class="download-card">
            <span>LINUX / X86_64</span><h3>Linux</h3>
            <p>The AppImage runs from your user directory without installation. The tarball contains the executable, libraries, and settings.</p>
            <div class="download-links">
              <a class="download-installer" data-release-asset="h5jive-linux-x86_64.AppImage" href="https://github.com/vrtulka23/h5jive/releases/latest/download/h5jive-linux-x86_64.AppImage">Download AppImage ↗</a>
              <a data-release-asset="h5jive-linux-x86_64.tar.gz" href="https://github.com/vrtulka23/h5jive/releases/latest/download/h5jive-linux-x86_64.tar.gz">Download portable tarball ↗</a>
            </div>
          </article>
          <article class="download-card">
            <span>MACOS / APPLE SILICON</span><h3>Mac · Apple Silicon</h3>
            <p>Open the DMG and copy H5Jive to your own Applications folder. The tarball contains the portable executable and settings.</p>
            <div class="download-links">
              <a class="download-installer" data-release-asset="h5jive-macos-aarch64.dmg" href="https://github.com/vrtulka23/h5jive/releases/latest/download/h5jive-macos-aarch64.dmg">Download DMG ↗</a>
              <a data-release-asset="h5jive-macos-aarch64.tar.gz" href="https://github.com/vrtulka23/h5jive/releases/latest/download/h5jive-macos-aarch64.tar.gz">Download portable tarball ↗</a>
            </div>
          </article>
          <article class="download-card">
            <span>MACOS / INTEL</span><h3>Mac · Intel</h3>
            <p>Open the DMG and copy H5Jive to your own Applications folder. The tarball contains the portable executable and settings.</p>
            <div class="download-links">
              <a class="download-installer" data-release-asset="h5jive-macos-x86_64.dmg" href="https://github.com/vrtulka23/h5jive/releases/latest/download/h5jive-macos-x86_64.dmg">Download DMG ↗</a>
              <a data-release-asset="h5jive-macos-x86_64.tar.gz" href="https://github.com/vrtulka23/h5jive/releases/latest/download/h5jive-macos-x86_64.tar.gz">Download portable tarball ↗</a>
            </div>
          </article>
        </div>
        <p class="download-note">All downloads are precompiled. Portable bundles need no installation. <a data-release-checksum href="https://github.com/vrtulka23/h5jive/releases/latest/download/SHA256SUMS">Verify downloads with SHA256SUMS ↗</a></p>
        <div class="perks-grid" aria-label="Why H5Jive">
          <article class="perk"><span>BUILT WITH DEAR IMGUI</span><h3>Native, responsive UI</h3><p>Plugin panels use the same immediate mode desktop interface as H5Jive's data inspector.</p></article>
          <article class="perk"><span>NO ADMIN RIGHTS</span><h3>Install in your space</h3><p>Precompiled downloads run from your own directory. The Windows setup installer uses a per-user install.</p></article>
          <article class="perk"><span>X11 SUPPORT</span><h3>Work remotely</h3><p>On Linux, H5Jive can use OpenGL for SSH forwarded X11 sessions when a compatible graphics stack is available.</p></article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="data" class="data-band">
        <div class="wrap data-content"><div><p class="eyebrow">REAL DATA, REAL FOOTPRINTS</p><h2>Scan lines you<br />can actually see.</h2><p>Explore the GOME-2 Band 3 sample in the source repository, with 15,574 valid geolocated pixels and measured radiance across 64 spectral channels. Each pixel retains its center coordinates, four corners, and scan direction.</p><a class="button light" href="./guide/">Open the guide <span>→</span></a></div>
          <div class="data-card"><div class="card-label">IN THE EXAMPLE FILE</div><div class="data-row"><span>Instrument</span><b>GOME-2 / MetOp-B</b></div><div class="data-row"><span>Orbit</span><b>32260 · 2013-01-06</b></div><div class="data-row"><span>Variable</span><b>Band 3 radiance</b></div><div class="data-row"><span>Footprint corners</span><b>4 per pixel</b></div><div class="card-source">Contains modified EUMETSAT Metop-B GOME-2 Level 1B data (2013). © EUMETSAT 2013. <a href="https://www.eumetsat.int/legal-framework/data-policy">Data policy</a> · <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">CC BY 4.0</a></div></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="plugins" class="section wrap plugin-section">
        <div class="section-intro"><div><p class="eyebrow">PLUGIN LAB</p><h2>Your science,<br />inside H5Jive.</h2></div><p class="section-note">Reuse H5Jive's HDF5 and NetCDF access, dataset selection, and visualization. Keep your analysis in its own plugin.</p></div>
        <div class="feature-list">
          <article class="feature"><span class="feature-n">01</span><div><h3>Download the source code</h3><p>Clone the open source project and try the comparison, dataset manipulation, and spatiotemporal subset demos in <code>examples/plugins/</code>.</p></div></article>
          <article class="feature"><span class="feature-n">02</span><div><h3>Implement your plugin</h3><p>You can ask an AI coding agent: “Add a Plugin Lab tool that shows the mean of my selected HDF5 dataset. Reuse H5Jive's file API and visualization views. Add a separate DIPL setting and an example.” Review and test the generated code with your data; Rust experience is not required to begin.</p></div></article>
          <article class="feature"><span class="feature-n">03</span><div><h3>Share it with scientists</h3><p>Propose your plugin as a pull request to the <a href="https://github.com/vrtulka23/h5jive/tree/main/plugins">Plugin Lab catalog</a> in the source repository. Other researchers can build on your analysis.</p></div></article>
        </div>
        <div class="plugin-actions"><a class="button primary" href="./plugins/">Explore Plugin Lab <span>→</span></a><a class="text-link" href="./guide/plugin-lab.html">Build and submit a plugin <span>→</span></a></div>
      </section>

      <section class="closing wrap"><img class="closing-icon" src="./h5jive.png" width="82" height="82" alt="" /><div><p class="eyebrow">OPEN THE PROJECT</p><h2>Start with a dataset.<br /><em>See where it leads.</em></h2></div><div class="closing-actions"><a class="button primary" href="./guide/">Read the guide <span>→</span></a><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/vrtulka23/h5jive">Browse source <span>↗</span></a></div></section>
    </main>
    <footer class="footer wrap"><a class="brand" href="#top"><img class="brand-icon" src="./h5jive.png" width="32" height="32" alt="" /> H5Jive</a><span>Dig into your data.</span><span>© H5Jive contributors</span></footer>
  </body>
</html>

